<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Two links, one actuator · Control Lab</title><style>
*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#edf2f5;color:#173443;font:15px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif}main{max-width:1200px;margin:24px auto;padding:34px;background:white;border-radius:24px}a{color:#087e82}h1{font-size:clamp(30px,5vw,48px);letter-spacing:-1.6px;line-height:1.1;margin:16px 0}h2{font-size:19px;margin:0}.eyebrow{font-size:11px;letter-spacing:2px;color:#008780}.intro{max-width:730px;color:#617782}.controls{display:flex;align-items:end;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:16px;padding:18px;background:#edf5f5;border-radius:14px;margin:25px 0}label{display:grid;gap:5px;font-size:12px}button,select{padding:11px 16px;border:1px solid #c8d9dd;border-radius:9px;background:white;color:#173443;font:inherit;cursor:pointer}button.primary{background:#173443;color:white}.time{flex:1;min-width:180px}input{width:100%;accent-color:#07867e}.pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px}.panel{border:1px solid #e1e9ed;border-radius:15px;padding:18px;min-width:0;background:#f9fbfc}.panel canvas{display:block;width:100%;height:320px}.status{font-size:12px;min-height:20px;margin:6px 0;color:#637b85}.plots{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:18px;margin:22px 0}.plots canvas{width:100%;height:215px;display:block}figure{margin:0;min-width:0}figcaption{font-weight:600}.legend{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:20px;font-size:12px;margin:18px 0}.legend i{display:inline-block;width:20px;border-top:3px solid;vertical-align:middle;margin-right:6px}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:13px}td,th{text-align:left;padding:12px 10px;border-bottom:1px solid #dfe7eb}.note{font-size:12px;color:#607782}details{padding:15px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #dfe7eb}summary{font-weight:600;cursor:pointer}code{background:#edf3f6;padding:3px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}footer{margin-top:22px;font-size:12px;color:#607782}@media(max-width:800px){.plots{grid-template-columns:1fr}}@media(max-width:650px){main{padding:18px;margin:6px}.pair{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style></head><body><main><a href="index.html">← Single-pendulum laboratory</a><div class="eyebrow" style="margin-top:24px">CONTROL LAB / TWO LINKS, ONE ACTUATOR</div><h1>Balancing a second pendulum.</h1><p class="intro">A single horizontal force must control the cart and two articulated links. Watch how correcting one angle affects the other. These are saved nonlinear simulations. Start hanging down, or explore recovery near the upright equilibrium.</p>
<p><a href="triple.html">Explore the triple pendulum →</a></p><div class="controls"><label>Experiment<select id="case"><option value="swingup" selected>Start hanging down · swing up and balance</option><option value="aligned">Both links lean right · +3° / +3°</option><option value="opposed">Links lean in opposite directions · +3° / −3°</option><option value="push">External push · 3 N for 0.2 s</option></select></label><button class="primary" id="play">Play</button><button id="reset">Restart</button><label class="time">Time <span id="time-label">0.00 s</span><input id="time" type="range" min="0" max="12" step=".02" value="0" aria-label="Time in seconds"></label></div>
<p id="explanation"></p><div class="pair"><section class="panel"><h2>Without feedback</h2><p class="status" id="open-status"></p><canvas id="open" role="img" aria-label="Uncontrolled double pendulum"></canvas></section><section class="panel"><h2 id="control-title">Planned swing-up + LQR</h2><p class="status" id="lqr-status"></p><canvas id="lqr" role="img" aria-label="Double pendulum stabilised by LQR"></canvas></section></div>
<p class="note">Both angles are measured from the upward vertical, not relative to the neighbouring link. Animation geometry is schematic. Near-upright experiments stop at 60° tilt or ±2 m cart travel. Swing-up permits full rotations and stops only at the travel limit. These are experiment cutoffs, not simulated impacts.</p>
<div class="legend"><span><i style="color:#15938b"></i>Lower link / cart / actuator</span><span><i style="color:#7964b8"></i>Upper link</span><span><i style="color:#b67c58;border-top-style:dashed"></i>Uncontrolled angles</span></div>
<div class="plots"><figure><figcaption>Two angles to balance</figcaption><canvas id="angles" role="img" aria-label="Both link angles with and without feedback over time"></canvas></figure><figure><figcaption>Cart position · controlled</figcaption><canvas id="position" role="img" aria-label="Controlled cart position over time"></canvas></figure><figure><figcaption>Actuator force · controlled</figcaption><canvas id="force" role="img" aria-label="Controlled actuator force over time"></canvas></figure></div>
<h2>What did the controller achieve?</h2><div style="overflow:auto"><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Settling time</th><th>Peak force</th><th>Squared-force effort</th></tr></thead><tbody id="metrics"></tbody></table></div><p class="note" id="comparison-note"></p>
<details open><summary>Starting from the bottom</summary><p>The near-upright LQR alone cannot reliably raise the pendulums from their hanging equilibrium. This experiment first follows an offline trajectory, designed with the nonlinear equations and force/travel bounds. A time-varying LQR corrects tracking errors. At 5 seconds, the controller switches to the upright LQR.</p><p>The displayed motion is integrated from the physical equations starting at rest with both angles at 180°. It is not a keyframe animation. The force plot shows the actual saturated actuator command. The two bobs begin below the cart; the first link is teal and the second is purple.</p></details><details open><summary>Why the second link changes the problem</summary><p>The controller sees six states: cart position and velocity, plus each link's angle and angular velocity. The links are coupled mechanically. The feedback law is <code>u = clip(−K s, −8, 8) N</code>. The gain is recomputed for this six-state system; it is not the gain from the single pendulum.</p><p id="gain"></p><p>The cart mass is 0.8 kg. Each point mass is 0.1 kg and each massless rod is 0.25 m long. Total suspended mass (0.2 kg) and upright height (0.5 m) match the single-pendulum example, but their mass distributions differ.</p></details>
<details><summary>Read the experiment correctly</summary><p>LQR minimises the linear-model objective ∫(sᵀQs + Ru²)dt, with Q = diag(10, 1, 100, 1, 100, 1) in SI state units and R = 0.1. All six states are measured perfectly. The simulation uses the full nonlinear equations, cart friction 0.08 N·s/m and gravity 9.81 m/s².</p><p>Settling requires |x| ≤ 0.02 m, |v| ≤ 0.03 m/s, both angles ≤ 1° in magnitude and both angular speeds ≤ 0.05 rad/s for the rest of the 12-second run, with at least 1 second remaining. Push recovery is reported from the start: subtract 4.2 s for time since the push ended. Swing-up settling must occur after the 5-second handoff.</p><p>Effort is ∫u²dt in N²·s, not energy in joules. The external push is additional to the actuator force and is not included in that effort. Numerical integration uses RK4 at 0.0025 s; playback interpolates samples at 0.02 s.</p><p>These cases demonstrate local stabilisation, not global stability or a maximum recoverable angle. The swing-up result covers one planned nominal manoeuvre. No sensor noise, actuator delay, joint friction or hardware experiments are included.</p></details><footer>English educational experiment · Python, full-resolution results and a research log accompany this page. <a href="../README.md">Project guide</a></footer></main>
<script id="data" type="application/json">__DATA__</script><script>
(()=>{'use strict';const D=JSON.parse(document.getElementById('data').textContent),$=id=>document.getElementById(id);let c,t=0,playing=false,last=0,raf=0;const teal='#15938b',purple='#7964b8';
function sample(rows,time){if(time<=rows[0][0])return rows[0];if(time>=rows.at(-1)[0])return rows.at(-1);let i=Math.min(rows.length-2,Math.floor(time/.02));while(i>0&&rows[i][0]>time)i--;while(i<rows.length-2&&rows[i+1][0]<time)i++;const f=(time-rows[i][0])/(rows[i+1][0]-rows[i][0]);return rows[i].map((v,k)=>v+f*(rows[i+1][k]-v))}
function canvas(id,h){const el=$(id),w=el.clientWidth,d=window.devicePixelRatio||1;if(el.width!==Math.round(w*d)||el.height!==Math.round(h*d)){el.width=Math.round(w*d);el.height=Math.round(h*d)}const ctx=el.getContext('2d');ctx.setTransform(d,0,0,d,0,0);ctx.clearRect(0,0,w,h);return[ctx,w,h]}
function rig(key){const [ctx,w]=canvas(key,320),row=sample(c[key].data,t),m=c[key].metrics,x=w/2+row[1]*(w-60)/4,y=155,L=62,x1=x+L*Math.sin(row[3]),y1=y-L*Math.cos(row[3]),x2=x1+L*Math.sin(row[5]),y2=y1-L*Math.cos(row[5]);ctx.strokeStyle='#bacdd6';ctx.lineWidth=2;ctx.beginPath();ctx.moveTo(15,y+26);ctx.lineTo(w-15,y+26);ctx.stroke();ctx.setLineDash([4,4]);ctx.beginPath();ctx.moveTo(w/2,y-10);ctx.lineTo(w/2,y+36);ctx.stroke();ctx.setLineDash([]);ctx.fillStyle='#173443';ctx.fillRect(x-26,y-5,52,22);for(const dx of [-17,17]){ctx.beginPath();ctx.arc(x+dx,y+22,6,0,2*Math.PI);ctx.fill()}for(const [a,b,xx,yy,col] of [[x,y,x1,y1,teal],[x1,y1,x2,y2,purple]]){ctx.strokeStyle=col;ctx.lineWidth=5;ctx.beginPath();ctx.moveTo(a,b);ctx.lineTo(xx,yy);ctx.stroke();ctx.fillStyle=col;ctx.beginPath();ctx.arc(xx,yy,9,0,2*Math.PI);ctx.fill()}ctx.fillStyle='#173443';ctx.font='12px system-ui';ctx.textAlign='center';ctx.fillText(`θ₁ ${(row[3]*180/Math.PI).toFixed(1)}°    θ₂ ${(row[5]*180/Math.PI).toFixed(1)}°    x ${row[1].toFixed(2)} m`,w/2,309);$(key+'-status').textContent=t>=m.end_s&&m.status!=='completed'?`Stopped at ${m.end_s.toFixed(2)} s · ${m.status==='tilt_limit'?'angle limit':'travel limit'}`:`Actuator ${row[7].toFixed(2)} N${$('case').value==='swingup'?(key==='open'?' · hanging freely':t<5?' · tracking the swing-up':' · upright LQR'):''}${$('case').value==='push'&&t>=4&&t<4.2?' · external push +3 N':''}`}
function plot(id,series,unit){const [ctx,w]=canvas(id,215),l=53,r=w-12,top=16,bottom=173;const vals=series.flatMap(s=>c[s.key].data.map(row=>row[s.col]*s.factor));vals.push(0);let low=Math.min(...vals),high=Math.max(...vals),pad=Math.max(.1,(high-low)*.1);low-=pad;high+=pad;const X=v=>l+v/12*(r-l),Y=v=>bottom-(v-low)/(high-low)*(bottom-top);ctx.font='11px system-ui';ctx.fillStyle='#617782';ctx.strokeStyle='#dce7eb';ctx.lineWidth=1;ctx.strokeRect(l,top,r-l,bottom-top);for(let i=0;i<=4;i++){let v=low+(high-low)*i/4;ctx.textAlign='right';ctx.fillText(v.toFixed(1),l-6,Y(v)+4);ctx.textAlign='center';ctx.fillText(i*3,X(i*3),bottom+17)}ctx.fillText('Time (s)',(l+r)/2,209);ctx.textAlign='left';ctx.fillText(unit,l,11);for(const s of series){ctx.strokeStyle=s.color;ctx.lineWidth=2;ctx.setLineDash(s.key==='open'?[4,4]:[]);ctx.beginPath();c[s.key].data.forEach((row,i)=>{if(i)ctx.lineTo(X(row[0]),Y(row[s.col]*s.factor));else ctx.moveTo(X(row[0]),Y(row[s.col]*s.factor))});ctx.stroke()}ctx.setLineDash([]);ctx.strokeStyle='#173443';ctx.lineWidth=1;ctx.beginPath();ctx.moveTo(X(t),top);ctx.lineTo(X(t),bottom);ctx.stroke()}
function draw(){if(!c)return;$('time').value=t;$('time-label').textContent=t.toFixed(2)+' s';rig('open');rig('lqr');plot('angles',[{key:'open',col:3,factor:180/Math.PI,color:'#b67c58'},{key:'open',col:5,factor:180/Math.PI,color:'#a39aa9'},{key:'lqr',col:3,factor:180/Math.PI,color:teal},{key:'lqr',col:5,factor:180/Math.PI,color:purple}],'deg');plot('position',[{key:'lqr',col:1,factor:1,color:teal}],'m');plot('force',[{key:'lqr',col:7,factor:1,color:teal}],'N')}
function pause(){playing=false;cancelAnimationFrame(raf);$('play').textContent='Play'}
function choose(){pause();t=0;c=D.cases[$('case').value];$('explanation').textContent={swingup:'Both links start hanging straight down (180°), at rest. A planned 5-second manoeuvre raises them; upright LQR then maintains balance.',aligned:'Both links start at +3°. The target is upright, with the cart at x = 0 m.',opposed:'The lower link starts at +3° and the upper at −3°, both measured from vertical.',push:'Both links start exactly upright. A 3 N force pushes the cart from 4.0 to 4.2 s.'}[$('case').value];$('control-title').textContent=$('case').value==='swingup'?'Planned swing-up + LQR':'Six-state LQR feedback';let m=c.lqr.metrics;const row=(title,settle,peak,effort)=>`<tr><td>${title}</td><td>${settle===null?'Not settled':settle.toFixed(2)+' s'}</td><td>${peak.toFixed(2)} N</td><td>${effort.toFixed(2)} N²·s</td></tr>`;$('metrics').innerHTML=row($('case').value==='swingup'?'Double pendulum · swing-up + LQR':'Double pendulum · LQR',m.settling_s,m.peak_force_N,m.effort_N2s);if(c.single){m=c.single;$('metrics').innerHTML+=row('Single pendulum · responsive LQR',m.settling_time_s,m.peak_force_N,m.force_squared_integral_N2s)}$('comparison-note').textContent=c.single?'Illustrative 12-second comparison: same cart, suspended mass, height, actuator limit and disturbance/initial aligned tilt. Mass distribution, number of states and LQR objective differ; this is not a universal performance ranking.':$('case').value==='swingup'?'A 5-second offline reference is tracked with time-varying LQR, then upright LQR takes over. The uncontrolled system remains hanging. This is one verified manoeuvre, not a controller proven to swing up from every state.':'No equivalent single-link initial state exists for opposing angles. Only the double-pendulum result is shown.';draw()}
function tick(now){if(!playing)return;t=Math.min(12,t+Math.max(0,Math.min((now-last)/1000,.1)));last=now;draw();if(t>=12)pause();else raf=requestAnimationFrame(tick)}
$('play').onclick=()=>{if(playing)pause();else{if(t>=12)t=0;playing=true;last=performance.now();$('play').textContent='Pause';raf=requestAnimationFrame(tick)}};$('reset').onclick=()=>{pause();t=0;draw()};$('case').onchange=choose;$('time').oninput=e=>{pause();t=Number(e.target.value);draw()};document.addEventListener('visibilitychange',()=>{if(document.hidden)pause()});matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').addEventListener('change',pause);let timer;new ResizeObserver(()=>{clearTimeout(timer);timer=setTimeout(draw,80)}).observe(document.querySelector('main'));$('gain').textContent='K = ['+D.gain.map(v=>v.toFixed(3)).join(', ')+'] in the state order [x, v, θ₁, ω₁, θ₂, ω₂].';choose();})();
</script></body></html>
